      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOpenAI clients look for `usage.completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens`, but SGLang only emits the legacy top-level counter. SDK users miss the reasoning usage even when it was measured.\n\n## Changes\n\nDerive the standard nested field from the existing cumulative counter, so normal and streaming serialization stay in sync. Keep the legacy field for existing clients.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe new regression fails on main with the nested field missing. The fixed protocol module passes the existing CPU protocol suite, including dict/JSON serialization, missing/zero counts and cumulative updates. No model execution changes.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39980616129](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39980616129)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39980616169](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39980616169)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39980616217](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39980616217)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
